{"parentUuid":"88380ebd-31eb-47d6-afb7-501e66afb508","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e135d9ad-cba2-4036-83a3-6f5d0216b138","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa6055acd1b6e26f5</task-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/aa6055acd1b6e26f5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement VR-2 slice 1\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Slice 1 of VR-2 is implemented in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/vr2` and every test and gate I ran passes; nothing is committed. Two deviations from the plan need your attention: the kill mechanism, and `harness.test.ts`, which I left untouched.\n\n## Files\n- **New:** `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts` (370 lines), `cli/src/core/verify_worker.ts` (59), `cli/test/verify_service.test.ts` (289), `cli/test/mcp_verify.test.ts` (350).\n- **Edited:** `cli/src/mcp.ts` (+103), `cli/src/index.ts` (+16, `serve-mcp` action only), `cli/src/config.ts` (one `export`), `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` (+32), `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` (+4).\n- `verify.ts` and `verify_contract.ts` are unchanged.\n\n## Worker launch\n- The service uses `child_process.fork`, detached, with stdout ignored and an IPC channel. The worker file extension follows the service module's own (`.ts` or `.js`).\n- **Source mode:** `execArgv` is set explicitly to `[\"--import\", import.meta.resolve(\"tsx\")]`, so it does not rely on inheriting flags. Proven by the tests (Node 24 only; Node 22 not run).\n- **Dist mode:** `execArgv` is `[]`. I checked this once by hand: built `dist`, got VERIFIED over stdio, then removed the build.\n- The worker sends `ready` before the job is sent, and messages are tagged, because tsx also talks on the IPC channel.\n\n## Security properties and their tests\nAll in `mcp_verify.test.ts` over real stdio unless noted.\n- **No arguments:** 23 hostile `arguments` values and extra `params` members each get `-32602`, with no receipt and no worker started.\n- **Operator verifier only:** with no `--authoritative-verifier`, the result is BLOCKED / `VERIFIER_NOT_APPROVED`, `runs: []`, and a marker file the repo's test script would create is absent. The server sends no requests to the client.\n- **Pinned base:** a weakened test committed after the pin gives BLOCKED / `VERIFICATION_EDIT_BLOCKED` (`verify_service.test.ts`). A second test documents the boundary: one committed before the pin becomes the reported base.\n- **Verdicts:** good diff VERIFIED, weakened test BLOCKED, broken product UNVERIFIED / `VERIFIER_FAILED`.\n- **Sandbox:** the VERIFIED receipt records a confined engine with network off.\n- **Refusals:** `--read-only`, `--mode read-only`, managed `require_human = [\"exec\"]`, and a workspace with no commit each return `isError` with no receipt.\n- **Single flight:** two calls in one chunk; the second is refused as busy and the first completes.\n- **Timeout and cancel:** the watchdog (service test) and `notifications/cancelled` (MCP test) both leave the worker and the `sleep` verifier gone, no receipt and scratch directories removed. A cancelled call gets no response.\n- **Size cap, receipts:** an oversized result is an error. Ids, eviction at 32, frozen receipts, the SHA-256, forged ids and byte-identical re-reads are covered in both files.\n\n## Results\n- `verify_service`: 10 pass, 0 fail. `mcp_verify`: 6 pass, 0 fail.\n- **Stress:** each file 5 of 5 sequential and 4 of 4 concurrent, all passing.\n- **Regression:** `mcp` 4/0, `mcp_http_delivery` 6/0, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3/0, `verify_command` 18/0, `verify_hostile` 46/0, `verify_sandbox` 10/0, `verify_schema` 4/0, `check_requirements` 28/0, `context_convergence` 57/0, the two `McpServer` tests in `harness.test.ts` 2/0.\n- **Gates:** `tsc --noEmit` clean; `check_invariants.mjs` and `check_requirements.mjs` exit 0. No gate required a ledger entry.\n\n## Deviations\n1. **Kill by process tree, not process group alone.** The verifier runs under `timeout`, which leaves the worker's group, so killing the group does not reach it. The service lists the worker's descendants with `ps` and signals each by pid, plus the group: SIGTERM first, SIGKILL after 10 s.\n2. **`harness.test.ts` not edited.** It has a live claim (codex, PA-4). The equivalent assertion is in `mcp_verify.test.ts`.\n3. **MCP test starts the server through `cliEntry()`** (the build when current, else source) to stay under the 300 s per-file CI limit. Locally the file takes about 175 s from source.\n4. **Small additions beyond the plan:** `watchdogMs` and `killGraceMs` test seams; `--mode read-only` treated as read-only; an `operator_hint` for REGRESSION_FREE with no deliverables; `_meta` allowed in `params`.\n5. **`config.ts` is imported dynamically inside the `serve-mcp` action**, to keep the `index.ts` edit within that command.\n\n## Not done\n- Node 22 was not run.\n- If the server is SIGKILLed, the worker stops only after its current verifier run ends.\n- The `INVARIANTS.md` row and the evidence doc are left for slice 3.\n- `test_durations.json` has no entry for the new files (a missing entry is not a failure).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>224224</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>47</tool_uses><duration_ms>2449587</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"6a4740a7-de1f-42b7-aad8-aa37769dc244","timestamp":"2026-11-23T19:59:57.517Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwtow6ew-a56b3d80"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":38,"turnIndex":229},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"