space, change git config/hooks/attributes/filters, move HEAD/the pinned base (`git commit --amend`, `git reset`, `git update-ref`, replace refs, grafts, a shallow file), alter `.git/info`, plant `node_modules/.bin` shims on PATH for the verifier, or environment files? The PR admits a same-user limit (documented in docs/MCP_GUIDE.md); judge whether the documentation is honest and complete, and separately whether any tamper route makes a result say VERIFIED that the *design* claims to prevent (pinned base, verification-path protection from VR-1). Distinguish \"documented limit\" from \"undocumented hole\".\n3. Pinned base: weakened tests committed after server start are judged against the pin. Try: commit weakened tests then `git update-ref` the pinned SHA's branch, rewrite history so the pinned SHA is unreachable/garbage-collected, replace objects (`git replace`), change `core.worktree`/`GIT_DIR` via repo config. What does the result say in each case — it must never be VERIFIED for a weakened test.\n4. Sandbox always on, network off; refusals in read-only mode, managed policy `require_human` for exec (see `cli/src/core/policy_runtime.ts`), no-commit workspace. Any way the caller flips these via workspace files?\n5. Single flight, watchdog timeout, cancellation (`notifications/cancelled`): worker and all verifier children gone; no orphan after server exit by stdin EOF and by SIGTERM; no scratch dirs left. Kill logic lists descendants with `ps` and signals pids: check for pid-reuse/race hazards and that it can never signal a process that is not a descendant (e.g. pid 1, the server itself, the caller).\n6. Receipts: unguessable ids, in-memory cap/eviction, cannot be created/overwritten by the caller, the SHA-256 matches the served bytes, a receipt never claims more than the result. Does a receipt leak host paths, environment, or secrets from verifier output (check redaction vs what `nexus verify` CLI prints)?\n7. Worker launch: `fork` with `execArgv` `--import tsx` in source mode and plain in dist mode; is the worker path derived only from the service module's own location (not cwd/env/PATH)? Could a workspace file (e.g. a `tsx` or `node_modules` in the served workspace, NODE_OPTIONS, a `.npmrc`) change what code the worker loads?\n8. Tests: do they fail when the property is removed? Mutate (then `git checkout`) at least: accept an argument silently; allow a discovered verifier; drop the base pin; skip the kill; and run the affected test file. Run both new test files plus `test/mcp.test.ts`, `test/verify_hostile.test.ts`, `test/verify_command.test.ts` at head, one at a time.\n9. Anything in `cli/src/mcp.ts` changes that weakens existing MCP behaviour.\n\nMandatory rules:\n- Do NOT edit ~/nexus-code or existing worktrees. `git -C ~/nexus-code fetch origin && git -C ~/nexus-code worktree add --detach ~/nexus-wt/revvr2 4196a306c97152ff735498d7c6bdb5a0bcdd0c75`; `cp -a ~/nexus-code/cli/node_modules ~/nexus-wt/revvr2/cli/`; copy `~/nexus-wt/ls1b/core/target/release/{harness-core,nexus-tui}` into `~/nexus-wt/revvr2/core/target/release/`. Remove the worktree at the end (`git -C ~/nexus-code worktree remove --force ~/nexus-wt/revvr2`). No commits, pushes or GitHub comments.\n- Every run uses a throwaway HOME (`mktemp -d`); tests: `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -20` in the foreground (the MCP test file takes about 3 minutes; allow 9). To drive the server by hand: `HOME=<tmp> node cli/node_modules/tsx/dist/cli.mjs cli/src/index.ts serve-mcp -w <throwaway git repo> [--authoritative-verifier ...]` and speak newline-delimited JSON-RPC from a script kept in a separate scratch directory; see `cli/test/mcp_verify.test.ts` for the handshake and repo setup. Never read the real ~/.nexus, /etc/nexus or ~/.config/nexus. No live inference, no network.\n- Stop every process you start by its own pid; never `pkill -f`. Hard timeout on every experiment; no unbounded background loops. Aim to finish in about 45 minutes; an experiment that fails to converge twice is \"not confirmed\".\n- Shell is zsh (use `bash -c` for loops); output passes through `rtk` (use `rtk proxy <cmd>` if it looks filtered). The runner prints `ℹ pass` / `ℹ fail`.\n\nReport under 650 words: verdict (ACCEPT / ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS / REQUEST CHANGES) at the exact SHA; findings ranked with file:line, each marked confirmed-by-running or by-reading, and classified as blocking / non-blocking / documented limit; mutation results; test counts; what you did not check.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/a560b8addcc5bbf8d.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0b2982c4-1923-4cf4-8787-b0481f22af90","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"303db2793d6a2880392130d433c616fa88e46134ed044bb9e3f15d90c275165c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VR-2 slice 1 is implemented, committed and pushed (16 new tests pass, type check clean). I'm opening the PR now and sending it for independent review."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QLxiznJg8q79ph2ugDiCgX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vr2.md","content":"## What this adds\n\n`nexus serve-mcp` gains a tool, `nexus_verify`, that lets another harness ask Nexus to check the change in the served workspace and get back a verdict and a receipt id (plan unit VR-2, decision D20 at its default). This is slice 1 of three; the ACP extension and the evidence document follow.\n\n## What the caller controls: nothing\n\nThe MCP caller is untrusted.\n\n- The tool takes no arguments. Any argument (a verifier command, a path, a claimed outcome, an extra field) is rejected with `-32602` and nothing runs.\n- Only the verifier the operator named when starting the server runs (`--authoritative-verifier`, with `--deliverable-file` for deliverables). A verifier discovered in the repository is never approved on this surface: the result is BLOCKED / `VERIFIER_NOT_APPROVED` with nothing executed, and the caller is never prompted.\n- The base commit is pinned when the server starts. A weakened test committed afterwards is judged against the pinned base, not accepted as the new baseline.\n- The sandbox is always on with the network off. The call is refused in read-only mode, where managed policy requires a human for command execution, and in a workspace with no commit.\n- Every verdict, BLOCKED included, is a successful result with a receipt. An error comes back only when no verdict exists.\n\n## How it runs\n\n- `cli/src/core/verify_service.ts` calls the existing `verifyChange` in a forked worker (`verify_worker.ts`). `verify.ts` and the v3 result schema are unchanged: there is no second verification path.\n- One verification at a time per process, not queued. A watchdog and `notifications/cancelled` end the worker and its children; output is capped.\n- Receipts: `vr-` plus 32 random hex digits, in memory only (32 at most, oldest evicted), with the SHA-256 of the document. Read back through `resources/read nexus://verify-receipt/<id>`. There is no file store, because the caller can already write any file the server's user can.\n\n## Tests (16 new)\n\n`mcp_verify.test.ts` (6, over real stdio) and `verify_service.test.ts` (10): verdict and receipt for a good change; a weakened test and a broken product are not VERIFIED; 23 hostile argument shapes are refused with nothing run; an unapproved discovered verifier runs nothing; a weakened test committed after the pin is blocked; the refusals; single flight; timeout and cancellation leave no worker, no verifier child and no scratch directory; receipt ids, eviction, forged ids, byte-identical re-reads.\n\nRun locally on Node 24: both files 5 of 5 in sequence and 4 of 4 concurrently. Existing files unchanged in result: `mcp` 4, `mcp_http_delivery` 6, `mcp_tool_through_spine` 3, `verify_command` 18, `verify_hostile` 46, `verify_sandbox` 10, `verify_schema` 4, `check_requirements` 28, `context_convergence` 57. `tsc --noEmit`, `check_invariants.mjs` and `check_requirements.mjs` pass. Node 22 has not been run locally; CI covers it.\n\n## Limits, stated plainly\n\n- The guarantee covers the request. A caller that can run commands as the server's user (and `serve-mcp` already offers `run_command`) can still tamper with `node_modules`, git configuration or the Nexus installation. Only OS isolation prevents that; the docs say so.\n- A commit made before the server starts becomes the base. Start the server at the commit you want changes judged against.\n- If the server is killed with SIGKILL, the worker stops only when its current verifier run ends.\n\n## Deviations from the plan\n\n- Timeout and cancel signal the worker's whole process tree by pid, not only its process group: the verifier runs under `timeout`, which leaves the group.\n- `harness.test.ts` is not edited (another agent holds it); the equivalent assertion is in `mcp_verify.test.ts`.\n- In `cli/src/index.ts` only the `serve-mcp` command changed.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was queried: no corpus project exposes verification as an MCP tool or an ACP extension. The plan (`VR2_PLAN.md`, reference-coding section) records the queries; the tool's refusal of all arguments follows from this repo's own VR-1 hardening rather than from a peer.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RstNY6K7Wir36yj2eqxbmd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/vr2-verify-for-clients --title \"feat(verify): nexus_verify, verification as an MCP tool (VR-2, slice 1)\" --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/pr_vr2.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) PR (claude-invariants-audit, VR2_VERIFY_FOR_CLIENTS): opened VR-2 slice 1 (nexus_verify MCP tool + verify service/worker) from ~/nexus-wt/vr2 at 4196a306. Independent review running; I do not merge it before the verdict.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Open the VR-2 slice 1 PR and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XHntFFBgxw6L7YiTEtcPcg","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review VR-2 slice 1 PR","subagent_type":"reviewer","prompt":"Independent security review of a GitHub PR in the repo at ~/nexus-code: branch `v1/vr2-verify-for-clients`, head `4196a306c97152ff735498d7c6bdb5a0bcdd0c75`, base `release/v1.3.0` (find the PR with `gh pr list --head v1/vr2-verify-for-clients`; `gh pr diff <n>`;