{"type":"data-flow-records","v":1,"sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","records":[{"response_id":"msg_011ChLTXnqHukSczjHwJ4Q5d","mark_sent_by":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","listed":["msg_011ChLTXHWgf48DPpg3jqChG"]}]}
{"parentUuid":"38394b4a-caf2-46f1-b2e2-718b0560a4e5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLTXnqHukSczjHwJ4Q5d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Status at about 20:15Z:\n\n- **VR-2 slice 1 is open as #756** and under independent review, with a brief to break it; CI is running. I won't merge it before the verdict.\n  - **What it adds:** an MCP tool, `nexus_verify`, on `nexus serve-mcp`. An untrusted caller can ask Nexus to verify the change in the served workspace and gets back a verdict and a receipt id.\n  - **Caller controls nothing:** the tool takes no arguments, only the verifier the operator configured runs, the base commit is pinned at server start, and the sandbox is always on with the network off.\n  - **Tests:** 16 new tests pass and were stable under repeated and concurrent runs on Node 24; the existing verification and MCP test files are unchanged in result. Node 22 is left to CI.\n  - **Stated limit:** a caller that can already run commands as the server's user (and `serve-mcp` offers that) can tamper with the environment itself. The docs say so.\n- **#755 (docs, another session's)** was opened against `main`. I retargeted it to `release/v1.3.0` under your release-branch rule and left a note on it. It revises the Power of Ten plan and records owner decisions I can't verify (no second reviewer, independent approval deferred). It merges when its checks are green unless you object.\n- **Release branch:** green at `f4333a35`.\n\nNext: act on the #756 review, then VR-2 slice 2 (the ACP extension method) once Codex confirms it is no longer editing the ACP files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":408770,"output_tokens":509,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":825,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":408770,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":825},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLTXnceXYDiMw1nAWoic","requestRef":"0b5e26cd-23fb-4d70-9352-6755b8fa0e09","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad55c61a-689d-4c44-b366-1d2a78812b6a","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:03:38.495Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
