test fails without the handler.\n\n2. In `startStdio`, the un-awaited `void this.handleMessage(req).then(...)` for the verify call has no `.catch`: a throw would be an unhandled rejection. Add a catch that writes a JSON-RPC error (-32603, with the request id) and never crashes the server.\n\n3. Read-only must be honoured however it was selected. Today `readOnly` for the verify tool is set only from `--read-only` / `--mode read-only` in the `serve-mcp` action. Also refuse when the effective configuration is read-only through the environment or config file (`REDACTED`, and whatever else `buildConfig`/`loadConfig` in `cli/src/config.ts` resolves to `approvalMode === \"read-only\"` or `readOnly`). Derive it from the same resolution the rest of the CLI uses (see how the `acp` command in `cli/src/index.ts` calls `buildConfig(program.opts())`), still editing only the `serve-mcp` command in index.ts. Add a test case to the existing refusals test: `REDACTED` in the server's env → `nexus_verify` is refused with no receipt. Make sure starting `serve-mcp` in an empty HOME with no model configured still works.\n\n4. Docs, `docs/MCP_GUIDE.md` \"What this does not protect against\": make the list complete and honest. Add: the server user's HOME (`~/.config/nexus/config.env` operator settings such as verifier environment passthrough, and any user-tier managed policy) can be edited by a client that runs commands as that user; an operator verifier script or binaries on PATH outside the workspace are equally writable by that user; a receipt's verifier output tail and paths are not secret from the client (it carries the workspace path and the verifier's output, as the CLI prints); and if the server is killed with SIGKILL the verifier runs on until its own timeout and scratch directories remain (SIGTERM/SIGINT now clean up). Update the `docs/USER_MANUAL.md` line only if it now says something untrue.\n\nThen re-run: `test/mcp_verify.test.ts` 3 times in a row, `test/verify_service.test.ts` once, `test/mcp.test.ts`, `tsc --noEmit`, `node scripts/check_invariants.mjs`. Report file:line of each change, the test names added, pass/fail counts, and anything you could not do."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
