{"parentUuid":"70065b07-0200-47ae-b7a9-81a68bc390e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLcdcXdX7unzKkMpUoSk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PjsVwo9dzPBAKSt3ekxmPJ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev757.md","content":"**Review at `f40c2974` — REQUEST CHANGES (docs only; three rows claim more than the release branch holds)**\n\nThe inventory is useful and its framing is right (no tag, qualification pending). These rows do not match `release/v1.3.0` at `56e644cf` and should be corrected before this is the record a release decision is made from:\n\n1. **GV-5 is listed as Landed; it is partial.** `approval.strict` is enforced, but `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md:30-31` on the release branch marks `mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow` and `plugins.disable_workspace` as \"not yet … Planned (GV-5)\", and line 7 says a key marked \"not yet\" \"is accepted and merged, and changes nothing\". \"Allowlists in schema\" is true and is not enforcement.\n2. **GV-1 is listed as Landed; slices 3 and 4 are open.** The same document says the `nexus policy` commands and the doctor findings are not in (lines 7, 349, 360), `sandbox.*` does not reach `nexus verify --sandbox` (37), and the TUI \"always\" answer under `approval.disable_auto` is planned (39). Partial, with those named.\n3. **VR-2 is listed as Landed with no caveat.** #756 merged with six open findings from its second review (posted on that PR): a new ACP session re-pins the verification base, the client chooses the verified directory and the result does not name it, id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` returns verification receipts, the interlocks are untested, the shutdown bound, `_meta`. Landed, follow-ups open.\n\nMissing rows: **SB-1**, **MT-1** and **MT-2** are plan units (Phase B and C) and do not appear; SB-1 and MT-2 have no PR. **PA-3** is filed under \"Stretch (may roll)\" while #758 is open for it and #706 already landed part of it.\n\nSmaller:\n\n- \"Merge queue: empty\" was true when written; #758 is open now. Either date the line or drop it.\n- G-3: \"full hostile matrix not re-audited here\" is honest; add that the gate as planned spans hooks, plugins and schedules, which do not exist yet, so it cannot be evaluated in full.\n- G-1: the real-server LSP suite and the real-project smoke run only on `main` by schedule. They were dispatched by hand on the release branch today (LSP: 14/14 after #751; smoke: pass). Worth a line, since #751 fixed a regression nothing else had caught.\n\nThe \"Deferred from a thin RC\" list is a scope proposal and is the owner's to accept; with the corrections above it should name GV-1 slices 3–4 and the GV-5 allowlists as either in or out.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2840,"cache_read_input_tokens":456741,"output_tokens":1743,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":296},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2840,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1743,"cache_read_input_tokens":456741,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2840,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2840},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10607,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PjsVwo9dzPBAKSt3ekxmPJ":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev757.md","content":"**Review at `f40c2974` — REQUEST CHANGES (docs only; three rows claim more than the release branch holds)**\n\nThe inventory is useful and its framing is right (no tag, qualification pending). These rows do not match `release/v1.3.0` at `56e644cf` and should be corrected before this is the record a release decision is made from:\n\n1. **GV-5 is listed as Landed; it is partial.** `approval.strict` is enforced, but `docs/MANAGED_POLICY.md:30-31` on the release branch marks `mcp.allow`, `mcp.disable_workspace`, `plugins.allow` and `plugins.disable_workspace` as \"not yet … Planned (GV-5)\", and line 7 says a key marked \"not yet\" \"is accepted and merged, and changes nothing\". \"Allowlists in schema\" is true and is not enforcement.\n2. **GV-1 is listed as Landed; slices 3 and 4 are open.** The same document says the `nexus policy` commands and the doctor findings are not in (lines 7, 349, 360), `sandbox.*` does not reach `nexus verify --sandbox` (37), and the TUI \"always\" answer under `approval.disable_auto` is planned (39). Partial, with those named.\n3. **VR-2 is listed as Landed with no caveat.** #756 merged with six open findings from its second review (posted on that PR): a new ACP session re-pins the verification base, the client chooses the verified directory and the result does not name it, id-less `_nexus/receipt/get` returns verification receipts, the interlocks are untested, the shutdown bound, `_meta`. Landed, follow-ups open.\n\nMissing rows: **SB-1**, **MT-1** and **MT-2** are plan units (Phase B and C) and do not appear; SB-1 and MT-2 have no PR. **PA-3** is filed under \"Stretch (may roll)\" while #758 is open for it and #706 already landed part of it.\n\nSmaller:\n\n- \"Merge queue: empty\" was true when written; #758 is open now. Either date the line or drop it.\n- G-3: \"full hostile matrix not re-audited here\" is honest; add that the gate as planned spans hooks, plugins and schedules, which do not exist yet, so it cannot be evaluated in full.\n- G-1: the real-server LSP suite and the real-project smoke run only on `main` by schedule. They were dispatched by hand on the release branch today (LSP: 14/14 after #751; smoke: pass). Worth a line, since #751 fixed a regression nothing else had caught.\n\nThe \"Deferred from a thin RC\" list is a scope proposal and is the owner's to accept; with the corrections above it should name GV-1 slices 3–4 and the GV-5 allowlists as either in or out.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChLcdcJF2y8tb5dr7xkMw","requestRef":"7a4a0d7c-6e0a-4a55-a7f7-57680ef0d768","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"2b50ae5f-5a5a-4055-9672-9c713209ed84","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:03:07.790Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
