{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:08:23.725Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab967e62105976eab</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01MZrzGt2KY6dn8zqFRuWvow</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/ab967e62105976eab.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PR #758 PA-3 goals\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**The head moved while I reviewed.** I reviewed `8d5b546500eb782ed593f8ea2c2fbad03da859fa`. The PR head is now `7320b78a1e99729285998f87c1d2b815cd70d7f6`, which I did not review, so this verdict does not carry over to it.\n\n**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES at `8d5b546500eb782ed593f8ea2c2fbad03da859fa`.** The core PA-3 requirement is not met, and the new test does not test it.\n\n**Blocking**\n1. **Process restarts are not detected (confirmed by running).** The \"boot id\" is `/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id` (`operation_runner.ts:719`). It changes only on a host reboot, so a crash mid-turn or a clean exit followed by a restart on the same boot keeps the same id.\n   - A probe of `goalStatus` showed `{status:\"RUNNING\", activeBootId: &lt;current boot&gt;}` stays `RUNNING` with nothing driving it.\n   - A goal with no `activeBootId` (state written before this PR) also stays `RUNNING`.\n   - Only a different boot id pauses a goal (`goal.ts:50-56`). Where there is no `/proc` (macOS), nothing pauses at all.\n   - The plan wants a goal \"active from an earlier process\" to resume paused. A per-process nonce plus the existing lock-liveness check would fit, but `activeBootId` is only cleared for COMPLETE/CANCELLED/PAUSED (`operation_runner.ts:~762`). A clean exit in WAITING or BLOCKED keeps it.\n2. **The new test does not cover pause-on-boot (confirmed by mutation).** `goal_lifecycle.test.ts:~183` seeds the state as `PAUSED` with a pre-written stale reason, so `goalStatus` returns PAUSED without any new logic.\n   - I removed both stale-boot checks (`operation_runner.ts` and `goal.ts:50`). All 6 tests still passed.\n   - The test also returns early when `currentBootId()` is undefined, so it passes vacuously on hosts without `/proc`.\n   - No test seeds a `RUNNING`, `WAITING` or `BLOCKED` state with a foreign boot id, which is the case the PR exists for.\n   - There is no test for a corrupt or truncated state file, a legacy state, or two processes booting at once.\n\n**Non-blocking**\n- **Model output and tool calls cannot change the lifecycle (by reading).** `goalStatus` still requires a closed ledger, a passing verifier receipt and an independent ACCEPT. I deleted the reviewer and verifier checks and the existing completion test failed (5 pass, 1 fail). That test, not the new one, guards a model \"done\". The new test adds nothing for it. The new transitions are called only from `driveOperation` and `GoalOrchestrator.resume`/`pause`, so I found no path from model text or a tool result.\n- **Explicit resume and budgets (by reading, partly unchecked).** Resume is explicit: `prepare` clears the stale pause in `goal.ts:~271`. The diff touches no approval, budget or `policy_runtime.ts` code, so nothing is loosened. The P10 budgets are untouched. I did not confirm that resume re-checks them, and I did not trace the policy path.\n- **Pause reason is overwritten (by reading).** `goalStatus` shows `pauseReason ?? stale`, so a stale-boot reason can be replaced by an older operator reason.\n- **Schema (by reading).** `activeBootId` and `pauseReason` are optional, validated in `operation_schema.ts:229-234`, and need no migration. `CURRENT_OPERATION_SCHEMA_VERSION` is not bumped. An older build ignores the fields, so this is acceptable.\n- **State-file handling is unchanged.** The existing store quarantines invalid operations on load (`operation_runner_persistence.ts:~112`) and has a lock and atomic save. I did not test two processes booting at once or a truncated file.\n- **Style.** The diff adds `delete (state as any).activeBootId` casts (`operation_runner.ts:~762, ~768`). Several lines are dense.\n\n**Doc (`PA3_GOAL_LIFECYCLE.md`)**\nIt claims a goal left active \"from an earlier host boot\" shows as `PAUSED`. That matches the code, but no test shows it. The claim is also narrower than the plan's \"earlier process\", and the doc does not say that crashes without a reboot are not covered.\n\n**Test counts at `8d5b546500eb`** (each file run alone with a throwaway HOME): every `goal*.test.ts` and `operation*.test.ts` file passed with 0 failures. `goal_lifecycle` had 6 pass, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, and `operation_view` 34. `operation_view` timed out in my first run but passed on the base and on a rerun at head (35s), so I put it down to a transient slowdown.\n\n**Not checked**\n- The new head `7320b78a`.\n- Non-Linux behaviour.\n- A real two-process race.\n- P10 budget and policy re-checks on resume.\n\nThe review worktree is removed. No edits, commits or comments were made.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>47827</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>14</tool_uses><duration_ms>342299</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
