{"parentUuid":"c873e637-ecdc-4583-8aa7-4b40c51def04","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0579a4f0-1ec2-4ee4-bd4d-e539b736faed","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0163xDDJMkqo3bwf9ufr66wJ","type":"tool_result","content":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/758#issuecomment-7115384674","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5bdaed1a-094a-4528-8f86-b7b0aec44808","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:08:52.411Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/758#issuecomment-7115384674","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"gitOperation":{"pr":{"number":758,"url":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/758","action":"commented"}}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c873e637-ecdc-4583-8aa7-4b40c51def04","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","hash":"de7b22d67850b869bed3b882115b33d3c8de1f0fd158cae013bd8bb40699163e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012NAw2GfycVZmrE3WJ5PNNR","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev758.md","content":"**Independent review at `8d5b546500eb782ed593f8ea2c2fbad03da859fa` — REQUEST CHANGES. It applies to the current head `7320b78a` too: that commit adds rolled-up token usage (`goal.ts`, `goal_command.ts`, the doc) and touches neither the restart detection nor the test.**\n\n**Blocking**\n\n1. **A process restart is not detected; only a host reboot is** (confirmed by running). The \"boot id\" is `/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id` (`operation_runner.ts:719`), which changes when the machine reboots. A crash mid-turn, or a clean exit, followed by a restart on the same boot keeps the same id, so a goal left `RUNNING` stays `RUNNING` with nothing driving it (`goal.ts:50-56` pauses only on a different id).\n   - A state written before this PR has no `activeBootId` and also stays `RUNNING`.\n   - Where there is no `/proc` (macOS) nothing is ever paused.\n   - `activeBootId` is cleared only for COMPLETE, CANCELLED and PAUSED (`operation_runner.ts`, about line 762), so a clean exit in WAITING or BLOCKED keeps it.\n\n   The plan's acceptance is a goal active \"from an earlier process\" resuming paused. A per-process identity combined with the existing lock-liveness check would meet it; a missing identity on an active goal should be treated as stale.\n\n2. **The new test does not test pause-on-restart** (confirmed by mutation). `goal_lifecycle.test.ts`, about line 183, seeds the state already `PAUSED` with the stale reason written in, so the status comes back PAUSED without any of the new logic. With both stale-boot checks removed (`operation_runner.ts` and `goal.ts:50`), all 6 tests still pass. The test also returns early when the boot id is unavailable, so it passes without checking anything on such hosts. Needed: states seeded `RUNNING`, `WAITING` and `BLOCKED` with a foreign identity and with none, each coming back `PAUSED` with the reason, and an already paused, completed or cancelled goal left as it was.\n\n**Not blocking**\n\n- A model's \"done\" still cannot complete a goal: `goalStatus` requires a closed ledger, a passing verifier receipt and an independent ACCEPT, and deleting those checks fails the existing completion test. That protection comes from the existing test, not from this PR. No path from model text or a tool result to the new transitions was found (by reading).\n- `goalStatus` shows `pauseReason ?? stale`, so an older operator reason can hide the stale-restart reason.\n- The doc says a goal active \"from an earlier host boot\" shows as PAUSED. That matches the code and is narrower than the plan; it should say that a restart without a reboot is not covered, or the code should cover it.\n- `activeBootId` and `pauseReason` are optional and validated (`operation_schema.ts:229-234`); no migration is needed. The schema version is not bumped, which is acceptable for optional fields.\n- `delete (state as any).activeBootId` (two places): a typed optional field would avoid the casts.\n\n**Tests at `8d5b5465`:** every `goal*.test.ts` and `operation*.test.ts` file passes run alone (`goal_lifecycle` 6, `goal_ledger_propagation` 2, `operation_view` 34).\n\n**Not checked:** the token-usage commit `7320b78a` itself, non-Linux behaviour, two processes starting at once, a truncated state file, whether resuming a paused goal re-checks the P10 budgets and managed policy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0163xDDJMkqo3bwf9ufr66wJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/nexus-code && gh pr comment 758 --body-file /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b/scratchpad/rev758.md | tail -1; echo \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) REVIEW (claude-invariants-audit): #758 (PA-3) REQUEST CHANGES at 8d5b5465, applies to 7320b78a: 'boot id' is the kernel boot_id, so a process restart without a host reboot leaves a goal RUNNING (the plan's case); the new test seeds the state already PAUSED and passes with the logic removed. Not in the merge queue until fixed. Please do not merge it outside the queue.\" >> \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\"","description":"Post the review on PR 758 and log it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
