id that is still alive (a live child process, or this process) stayed RUNNING, so a second concurrent `nexus` is neither paused nor stolen.\n- Limits:\n  - A reused pid reads as alive, so the goal is never paused.\n  - A state on a different host, or with a pid but no host, stays RUNNING.\n  - A state with only the current `activeBootId` and no pid stays RUNNING.\n  - The reason text reads badly: \"left active by earlier process (pid N) is no longer running\" and \"left active by an earlier process left it active…\".\n\n**Blocker 2 (the test must exercise it): fixed for goals, with one gap.**\n- With `staleDriverReason` forced to return undefined, `goal_lifecycle.test.ts` went from all passing to 5 pass and 2 fail. I restored the file with `git checkout`.\n- The new same-boot test seeds RUNNING with a dead pid and does not need `/proc`.\n- The host-boot test still has `if (!boot) return;` at `goal_lifecycle.test.ts:187`, so it passes vacuously without `/proc`.\n- No test references `pauseForStaleDriver`, `stale_driver` or \"Paused on resume\" on the `driveOperation` path.\n\n**New finding, blocking: a regression in `driveOperation`.**\n- `cli/test/operation_entry_integrity.test.ts` (\"a stale snapshot … not written back over COMPLETE\") fails at head (2 pass, 1 fail; PAUSED instead of COMPLETE). On `origin/release/v1.3.0` the same file passes 3 of 3.\n- Cause: `operation.ts:570` plans operations as RUNNING with no identity. `driveOperation` now treats any \"existing\" RUNNING operation without identity as stale (`operation_runner.ts:~735-745`, rule \"no identity means stale\").\n- A freshly planned operation resumed through `operation_cli.ts:391`, `loop.ts:471` or `batch.ts:223` can therefore be paused without ever running.\n- Fix: apply the no-identity rule only in goal code. Alternatively, have `plan` stamp identity, or make `driveOperation` skip the rule when the operation has never run. Then add a `driveOperation` test for the stale path.\n\n**Non-blocking items:**\n- `pauseReason ?? stale` still hides the stale reason behind an older operator reason. Probed: RUNNING with a dead pid and an old `pauseReason` reports only the operator text. Not fixed.\n- The doc is more accurate now, but it does not list the limits above (pid reuse, other host).\n- The `(state as any)` casts remain and have multiplied (`operation_runner.ts:784-792`, plus the new `catch (err: any)`). Use a typed optional delete instead.\n\n**Item 4 (lifecycle and policy):**\n- The delta only reads the identity fields and the pid. No model text, tool call or workspace content can set them.\n- `policy_runtime.ts` is untouched.\n- `goal.ts:352` pauses on the stale reason, and resume goes through the same `driveOperation` path as start. I did not run an approval or budget check against it.\n\n**Item 5 (token usage, `7320b78a`):**\n- It only reads `tokenStats` totals and counts, and exposes no content.\n- Reported and estimated tokens are split, so nothing is double counted across the two buckets.\n- It reloads one task file per unit on every `result()` call, which is acceptable.\n- `agentRuns` sums `unit.runs`, which may include retries. That is cosmetic.\n\n**Test counts at head (throwaway HOME, one file at a time):**\n- `goal_ledger_propagation` 2/0\n- `goal_lifecycle` 7/0\n- `operation_account_identity` 14/0\n- `operation_concurrency` 16/0\n- `operation_entry_integrity` 2 pass / **1 fail** (passes 3/0 on base)\n- `operation_git` 42/0\n- `operation_lock` 9/0\n- `operation_messages` 8/0\n- `operation_release_acceptance` 4/0\n- `operation_release_review` 24/0\n- `operation_runner_execution_diagnostics` 3/0\n- `operation_runner_refactor` 3/0\n- `operation_runner_restart` 1/0\n- `operation_schema` 18/0\n- `operation_view` 34/0\n\n**Not checked:** Node 22 versus 24, behaviour on a host without `/proc`, a live two-process race, other test files, and CI status.\n\nBoth worktrees (`rev758b`, `rev758base`) were removed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>45852</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>275317</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
