{"parentUuid":"fe28fb90-309a-423a-ad53-7776f032aedc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"56ab2c9c-1360-4c32-850a-bf90c9e71973","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KoK5zjahjKNDeBwF3T92nn","type":"tool_result","content":"release/v1.3.0\tv1/p10-03-flight-log-integrity\t75\t11\tfix(audit): expose skipped flight log records\tcli/src/flight.ts,cli/test/hash_chain.test.ts,docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n## Summary\n\n- Mark flight recording as degraded when payload redaction or an append fails.\n- Return an explicit `recordingSkipped` event without stopping the authorized tool action.\n- Disable subsequent chaining, so the existing flight verifier reports broken or unchained evidence instead of accepting a later chain that omitted a record.\n- Correct the P10 plan to reuse existing GV-3 hash chains, GV-2 audit bundles, and candidate receipt binding, and record the remaining evidence-policy gaps.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was queried against the local `goose` and `opencode` indexes. Goose's stdio recorder returns `io::Result` and propagates recording I/O failures (`crates/goose-test/src/mcp/stdio/record.rs:63`); OpenCode destroys the recording stream on output errors (`packages/simulation/src/recording.ts:54`). I rejected propagating telemetry write failures through Nexus tool execution beca","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6a76899a-39ed-4088-8162-8ce7cea31f0c","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:17:21.421Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"release/v1.3.0\tv1/p10-03-flight-log-integrity\t75\t11\tfix(audit): expose skipped flight log records\tcli/src/flight.ts,cli/test/hash_chain.test.ts,docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n## Summary\n\n- Mark flight recording as degraded when payload redaction or an append fails.\n- Return an explicit `recordingSkipped` event without stopping the authorized tool action.\n- Disable subsequent chaining, so the existing flight verifier reports broken or unchained evidence instead of accepting a later chain that omitted a record.\n- Correct the P10 plan to reuse existing GV-3 hash chains, GV-2 audit bundles, and candidate receipt binding, and record the remaining evidence-policy gaps.\n\n## Reference coding\n\nXERJ was queried against the local `goose` and `opencode` indexes. Goose's stdio recorder returns `io::Result` and propagates recording I/O failures (`crates/goose-test/src/mcp/stdio/record.rs:63`); OpenCode destroys the recording stream on output errors (`packages/simulation/src/recording.ts:54`). I rejected propagating telemetry write failures through Nexus tool execution beca","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fe28fb90-309a-423a-ad53-7776f032aedc","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
