{"parentUuid":"701ff0f2-ad23-483c-992c-a1bba7dabe6d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011ChLyzmsVuwGvhJ7Fo139B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#765 is merged and the release branch is green at `4d9996d4`. No PRs are open.\n\nOne thing to flag about that merge: it wasn't mine. My merge call was refused with \"merge already in progress\", meaning another session merged the same PR in the same second. The outcome is the intended one, since the PR had my accept and green required checks, but two sessions merging at once is the race the queue exists to prevent. I've logged it and asked the other session, again, to stop or to say that you told it to merge.\n\n**What #765 changed:** docs only. They now state accurately what the inference budget doesn't cover: subagents, operation units, findings extraction and compaction calls are outside it; a project `.env` can raise the ceiling up to the hard maximum; and without durable state the counter is per turn. Those are the notes I left on #760.\n\n**What still stands between here and landing v1.3.0, unchanged**\n- **Unbuilt:** PF-3, PF-4, SB-1, MT-2, BG-1, BG-2, HK-1 to HK-3, PA-2.\n- **Unfinished:** GV-1 slices 3–4, the GV-5 allowlists, the six VR-2 follow-ups.\n- **Yours:** which units roll to v1.4, the go-ahead for the merge to `main` and the release-candidate tag, and who holds the merge queue."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":688,"cache_read_input_tokens":587205,"output_tokens":441,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":688,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":587205,"cache_creation_input_tokens":688,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":688},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011ChLyzm5NAS3Ms8pD6HR5r","requestRef":"c9055270-8b92-4c02-a585-71a62b3446a0","requestedModel":"claude-fable-5-2","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ebf735e1-f64e-4515-af5e-b5fb3094373a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:43:07.942Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","madeBy":"model","session_id":"d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","version":"2.1.329","gitBranch":"main","slug":"synthetic-moseying-seahorse","dataFlowOn":true}
