{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:12:19.225Z","sessionId":"43bcbb67-2cff-4fa8-a05e-f8aa598df73b","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa77b327dba41b9c2</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Am51M9bLBiyDWqzoNeX5iJ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/d25d0d24-8aed-4b03-a951-966dc54f0666/tasks/aa77b327dba41b9c2.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PR #766 complexity gate\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: ACCEPT WITH FOLLOW-UPS** at `23a563ff31383136d7ad3b93ec59410f39bac631`. The head did not move during the review.\n\n**1. Dependency**\n- Added `@babel/parser` pinned at 7.29.15 (`cli/package.json:43`, devDependencies only).\n- The lockfile gains four packages, all `\"dev\": true` and MIT: `@babel/types` 7.29.15, `helper-string-parser` 7.29.15, `helper-validator-identifier` 7.29.7.\n- None of the four has an install script (`hasInstallScript` is absent, and their `package.json` files carry no install hooks).\n- `scripts/package-linux.sh:66` uses `npm ci --omit=dev`, and the notices step runs `--production`. The new packages are therefore excluded from the tarball and from the notices.\n- `node scripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs cli/package-lock.json` passed (76 versions). The lockfile diff touches no `engines.node` field.\n- `@babel/*` was not in the main `cli/node_modules`. A sibling worktree (`p10-05-complexity`) had it, so I copied it read-only into my worktree. The check ran against exactly those versions, and I ran no npm commands.\n\n**2. Where the gate runs**\n- `Makefile:26` adds it to `make lint`. CI runs `make lint` only in `test-gates` (`ci.yml:98`), so it runs on Node 22 and 24.\n- It does not run in the packaging job or `release.yml`.\n- All checkouts use `fetch-depth: 0`, which the `git show` and `merge-base` calls need.\n- The check takes about 3.7 s. `release_workflow_parity` passes 6/6.\n\n**3. The check**\n- It measures cyclomatic complexity and maximum control nesting, plus line count (reported only).\n- \"Critical\" is a hand list in the baseline JSON. Any increase over the baseline revision's own source fails (exit 1). There is no threshold and no `--update` mode.\n- The baseline file is validated strictly, and bad input exits 2 (fail-closed). Duplicates are rejected, and the revision must be a 40-hex ancestor of `HEAD`.\n- A function that is missing or ambiguous throws, which exits 2. I renamed `driveOperation` and got rc=2 (confirmed by running).\n\n**Bypasses, ranked (all confirmed by running)**\n1. **Inline callbacks are excluded from the measurement** (`check_critical_complexity.ts` `measureNode`, which returns on any nested function). Moving a nested `if` into an inline arrow function left `driveOperation` at CC 17 / nesting 3 and rc=0. This is the cheapest bypass and is also a blind spot. **Non-blocking**, but the doc and metric comment should say it, or nested functions should be counted into their enclosing function.\n2. **`?.`, `||=`, `&amp;&amp;=` and `??=` are not counted.** Adding `q ||= 1; q ??= 2; state?.id?.length` gave rc=0 with no change. **Non-blocking.** Add `OptionalMemberExpression`, `OptionalCallExpression` and logical `AssignmentExpression`, or document the omission.\n3. Extracting a helper that is not on the list passes. The plan text states this. Line growth is also not enforced, by design.\n4. Editing `baselineRevision` or the function list in the same PR is possible, but it is visible in review. This is a known limit of a single-user repo.\n\n**4. Baseline**\n- It lists 5 functions, and `runTurnImpl` is covered. This is the only measured form of the baseline I checked: HEAD against baseline revision `4d9996d4` (the current base tip) gives CC 324/324, 288/288, 70/70, 17/17 and 17/17. Nesting is 5/6/4/3/3 and lines are 1262/900/209/63/47.\n- These numbers match the plan text. There is no regenerate mode, so there was nothing to diff.\n\n**5. Tests (3 pass, 0 fail)**\n- Making `compareMetrics` never flag a violation fails 1 test (confirmed by running).\n- Two mutations leave all three tests passing (confirmed by running). **Non-blocking:**\n  - Changing `main()` to always return 0 is not caught, because the CLI exit path is untested. Add a test that spawns the script on a fixture or checks `main()`'s return code.\n  - Making the check compare current source to current source is not caught, because baseline and current are identical today. A temp-repo fixture with a regressed function would catch it.\n- Deleting the gate from the `Makefile` passes `release_workflow_parity` (6/6), so nothing pins the wiring. Add a parity assertion that `make lint` contains the script.\n- The test file needs no network, only git history, which the shards have. It is absent from `test_durations.json`, and the sharder then falls back to file size (`test_shards.mjs:62`).\n\n**6. Runs at head** (throwaway HOME)\n- `critical_complexity` 3/3.\n- `release_workflow_parity` 6/6.\n- `leak_guard` 6/6.\n- `check_requirements` 28/28.\n- `tsc --noEmit` is clean.\n- `check_deprecated_lock` and `check_invariants` both pass.\n- The standalone gate prints rc=0.\n\n**7. Docs** (`POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:107`)\n- The numbers match, and the scope caveat (extracted helpers need separate assessment) is honest.\n- The acceptance wording still says \"crossing a threshold\", but the implementation is \"any increase over baseline\". Align the wording.\n- I could not verify \"zero vulnerabilities\" or \"Clippy and fmt passed\".\n\n**Not run**\n- cargo clippy and `make fmt-check`, which are the rest of `make lint`, were skipped as slow and unrelated to this PR's diff.\n- A fresh `npm ci` was not run, because there is no network.\n- No CI run was inspected.\n\nThe worktree `~/nexus-wt/rev766` has been removed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>43916</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>292880</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
